The quad cursor trail follows kitty's design -- four corners chasing the
cursor's at per-corner rates -- with kitty's defaults (decay 0.1 s and 0.4
s, a start threshold of two cells) and its half-pixel end. Its rate choice,
which had followed kitty's cursor_trail.c term for term, was re-derived on
2026-10-25 from the derivation in note W, section 8, after a line-by-line
audit against kitty v0.49.2, and so were the copies of it in four research
prototypes under note W; no line of kitty's is ported
  Files:   src/trail.rs
  Licence: none claimed; kitty is GPL-3.0-only
  Notice:  none needed
  Status:  kept: redistributable, and its notice is satisfied
  From:    https://github.com/kovidgoyal/kitty/blob/b2cb871254fbdac19a085188813c8dfb258b95cd/kitty/cursor_trail.c
